  "slug": "cryo-em-1743",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and papers apply unsupervised, zero-shot, and fidelity-constrained learning to noisy cryo-EM/ET and multiplexed imaging data.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is learned correction of noisy microscopy data, with several methods operating without labeled training targets. An unsupervised autoencoder preprint jointly optimizes particle pose and structure to classify cryo-EM/ET particles and separate contamination. CryoET-DDM, a diffusion model, denoises cryo-ET tilt series using noise patches drawn from the same tilt series and a fidelity-guided loss that preserves underlying features. SpillOT applies zero-shot optimal transport to spillover in highly multiplexed images, while ROOF uses semi-blind NMF to correct fluorescence bleed-through under a reference crosstalk matrix. ROOF lies outside cryo-EM but shares constrained decomposition of mixed imaging data. What is new is the use of same-sample noise statistics and fidelity constraints to guide learned denoising and classification.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
